#usda 1.0
(
    defaultPrim = "World"
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Z"
    doc = """UrbanTwin Phase 9 stage - open THIS for demos.

    Composes the PHASE 8 stage - the final city, which carries the Stressed /
    Intervention demoState variants and chains down through Phase 2 semantics
    to the Phase 1 geometry - and adds the Phase 9 layers on top: recovered
    building heights, OSM-derived materials, real sun shadows, an extended
    ground plane and saved demo cameras.

    Everything here is an `over`. No Phase 1-8 layer is modified, so the
    manifest hash and with it city_id stay valid.

    Two variant sets on /World:
      demoState  Stressed | Intervention   (Phase 8; phase8/switch_state.py)
      cityLook   realistic | analytic      (Phase 9; materials.usda)

    Generated overlays (path colours, agent instancer) are sublayered above
    when present; both are produced by the scripts in phase9/ and are
    optional - the stage opens fine without them.

    Viewport checklist before recording:
      - turn the viewport grid OFF and the HUD off, then deselect
      - pick /World/Cameras/Overview, Corridor or ProblemZone
      - RTX - Real-Time is enough; Path Traced looks better if it holds up"""
    subLayers = [
        @generated/agents.usda@,
        @generated/path_colors.usda@,
        @cameras.usda@,
        @materials.usda@,
        @heights.usda@,
        @look.usda@,
        @lighting.usda@,
        @../../phase8/scene/main.usda@
    ]
)

over "World"
{
}
